# Docs sync

When an attribute, option, method, event, CSS variable, preset or default changes, update **together**:
`src/index.js` · `src/marker.css` · `types/index.d.ts` · README (Attributes / JavaScript / Events / The marker / Browser support) ·
`llms.txt` · tests here · and in the sibling repo `../chapterize-js-site`: `site/pages/index.html` (attributes, API),
`site/pages/markers.html` (CSS variables), then its `npm test` (re-syncs `vendor/chapterize-js/`; commit that too).

`test/docs.test.mjs` fails if a `data-spy-*` attribute read in `src/`, a `--spy-*` variable in `marker.css` or a runtime
export is missing from README, `llms.txt` or `types/`; the site repo's `test/site.test.mjs` ("site docs accuracy") does
the same for its pages, reading this checkout. The README `## Frameworks` section is the single source for the site's `/frameworks`. Its Next.js recipe was verified in a real Next 16 app (2026-10-23): change it only with a re-check in a Next app.
Sizes in README/AGENTS/PROJECT-GOALS are measured numbers: re-measure with `npm run size`, don't guess.
Add a decisions-log entry to `docs/PROJECT-GOALS.md` (dated) for any product decision.
